{title: Many Rooms}
{subtitle: John 14:1–6}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 75}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb/D] | [Cm7] [Bb/D] | [Eb] [Bb/D] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
The lamps were [Eb]low in the [Bb/D]upper [Cm7]room
The bread was [Abmaj7]broken, the night came [Eb]soon
He told his friends that he [Bb/D]had to [Cm7]go
Their fa[Abmaj7]ces fell and [Bb]their hearts sank [Eb]low
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Do not [Ab]let your hearts be trou[Eb]bled
Trust in [Cm7]God, and trust in [Bb]me
In my Father's [Ab]house there are many [Cm7]rooms
I am [Ab]the way and the [Bb]truth and the [Eb]life
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Eb] | [Bb/D] | [Cm7] | [Eb] [Bb/D] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
I go a[Eb]head to make it [Bb/D]ready there [Cm7]
A place [Ab]for you, prepared with [Eb]care
I will come back and take you to [Bb/D]my[Cm7]self
So that where I [Ab]am, you may be al[Eb]so
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Do not [Ab]let your hearts be trou[Eb]bled
Trust [Cm7]in God, and trust in [Bb]me
In my Father's [Ab]house there are many [Cm7]rooms
I am [Ab]the way and the [Bb]truth and the [Eb]life
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Ab]Then Thomas spoke for all the [Cm7]rest
[Ab]With a worried heart and an honest [Cm7]guess
[Ab]Lord, we do not know where you are [Cm7]going
[Ab]How can we [Bb]know the [Eb]way?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
I am the [Ab]way and the [Bb]truth and the [Cm7]life
No one [Ab]comes to the Fa[Bb]ther except through [Eb]me
{end_of_bridge}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Do [Ab]not let your hearts be [Eb]troubled
Trust in God, [Ab]and [Bb]trust in [Eb]me
{end_of_verse}
